src/tables.rs holds the character classes of Python's `str` (isalpha, \w, lower, isspace), generated by
tools/gen_tables.py from the Unicode Character Database 17.0.0 as shipped with Python 3.15.2. The tables are
derived from the Unicode Data Files and are covered by the Unicode License v3 (SPDX: Unicode-3.0), whose
notice below stays with every copy of the source and with every binary distribution. The program `rangkern`
also contains the Unicode data tables of the crates unicode-normalization (licensed "(MIT OR Apache-2.0)
AND Unicode-3.0") and caseless (case folding data), both reached through notiz-kern; the same notice
covers them. `rangkern --licenses` prints this file.

